From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 05:48:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Advance the queue ordinal past a
 recovered job's commands

Every fully retired command advances its logical queue's completed
ordinal by compare-exchange, and the ordinal is shared by every job of
that queue. A passed abort under g16_recovery_tolerant fails its job
and never advances it, so the next job of the same queue misses the
exchange and the device fail-stops with EIO, as the injected recovery
showed (recovery 1, tolerated 1, then fail-stop).

With g16_recovery_tolerant, retiring a prefix of an aborted job now
advances the queue ordinal past its commands, so later jobs of the
queue continue the chain. Without the parameter nothing changes.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/poll.rs | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/poll.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/poll.rs
index 07eac2a0c8..155d5b68a8 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/poll.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/poll.rs
@@ -729,6 +729,14 @@ pub(crate) fn retire_oldest(
                     return;
                 }
             }
+        } else if params::recovery_tolerant() && f.job.aborted() {
+            // A passed abort (or a later prefix of its job) never completes its commands,
+            // but the queue's ordinal is shared by every job of that queue: advance it past
+            // these commands, so the queue's next job continues the chain instead of
+            // missing it and fail-stopping the device. The job itself has failed.
+            for index in f.first..f.first + f.count {
+                let _ = f.job.command_retired(index as u32);
+            }
         }
         if self.engine.flights.is_empty() {
             // Drained: a gap until the next publication.
